[[Governor of Delaware|Governor]] [[John Carney (Delaware politician)|John Carney]] was re-elected to a second term in [[2020 Delaware gubernatorial election|2020]] with 59.5% of the vote. He was [[Term limits in the United States|term-limited]] by the [[Delaware Constitution]] in 2024 and could not seek re-election for a third term. [[New Castle County, Delaware|New Castle County]] [[County Executive|Executive]] [[Matt Meyer]] defeated [[Lieutenant Governor of Delaware|Lieutenant Governor]] [[Bethany Hall-Long]] and President of the [[National Wildlife Federation]] and former secretary of the [[Delaware Department of Natural Resources and Environmental Control]] Collin O'Mara for the Democratic nomination and [[Delaware House of Representatives|state House]] [[Minority Leader]] [[Michael Ramone]] defeated Police Officer Jerry Price and Contactor Bobby Williamson for the Republican nomination.

Meyer comfortably won the election, albeit by the closest margin since [[2004 Delaware gubernatorial election|2004]]. Meyer's 56% of the vote is the lowest for the Democrats since that election, while Ramone's 44% is the highest since for Republicans.{{Election box begin no change|title=Democratic primary results<ref name="deprim">{{cite web |title=2024 Primary Election Report |url=https://elections.delaware.gov/results/html/index.shtml?electionId=PR2024 |website=Delaware Department of Elections |date=September 10, 2024 |access-date=September 18, 2024 |archive-date=December 11, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241211225142/https://elections.delaware.gov/results/html/index.shtml?electionId=PR2024 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}
