[[Governor of New Hampshire|Governor]] [[Chris Sununu]] won re-election to a fourth term in [[2022 New Hampshire gubernatorial election|2022]]. However, on July 19, 2023, he announced he would not seek re-election.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Astor |first=Maggie |date=2023-07-19 |title=Chris Sununu Won't Run for Re-Election as Governor of New Hampshire |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/19/us/politics/chris-sununu-new-hampshire-governor.html |access-date=2023-07-19 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Former [[U.S. Senator]] [[Kelly Ayotte]] won the Republican gubernatorial nomination, defeating former [[New Hampshire State Senate|state Senator]] [[Chuck Morse]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mueller |first=Julia |date=2024-09-11 |title=Former Sen. Kelly Ayotte wins GOP primary for New Hampshire governor |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4872711-new-hampshire-gop-primary-kelly-ayotte/ |access-date=2024-09-11 |website=The Hill |language=en-US}}</ref>

