[[Governor of North Carolina|Governor]] [[Roy Cooper]] was re-elected to a second term in [[2020 North Carolina gubernatorial election|2020]] with 51.5% of the vote. He was [[Term limits in the United States|term-limited]] by the [[North Carolina Constitution]] in 2024 and could not seek re-election for a third consecutive term. [[North Carolina Attorney General|Attorney General]] [[Josh Stein]] defeated former [[North Carolina Supreme Court|state Supreme Court]] justice [[Michael R. Morgan|Michael Morgan]] for the Democratic gubernatorial nomination, while [[Lieutenant Governor of North Carolina|Lieutenant Governor]] [[Mark Robinson (American politician)|Mark Robinson]] defeated [[North Carolina State Treasurer|State Treasurer]] [[Dale Folwell]] for the Republican gubernatorial nomination.<ref name=jsnc>{{Cite web |title=North Carolina AG Josh Stein launches bid for governor |first=Elena |last=Schneider |work=[[Politico]] |date=January 18, 2023 |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/01/18/north-carolina-ag-josh-stein-launches-bid-for-governor-00078281}}</ref><ref name=mmnc>{{Cite web |title=Former North Carolina justice enters Democratic primary for governor in 2024 |first=Hannah |last=Schoenbaum |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=September 12, 2023 |url=https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-governor-election-stein-morgan-democrats-da61d6f539276289d6b1d97c1d988985}}</ref><ref name=dfnc>{{cite web|last=Craver|first=Richard|title='Uniquely qualified': Winston-Salem native and NC Treasurer Dale Folwell will run for governor|url=https://journalnow.com/news/local/dale-folwell-governor-mark-robinsonforsyth-county-republican-party-convention/article_7905d408-cb0d-11ed-84ba-27ed0846f91d.html|work=The Winston-Salem Journal|date=March 25, 2023|access-date=March 25, 2023}}</ref><ref name="Mikkelsen">{{cite news |last1=Mikkelsen |first1=Emily |last2=Stamps |first2=Brayden |title=Lt. Gov. Mark Robinson announces run for governor at cloudy Ace Speedway rally |url=https://myfox8.com/news/politics/nc-gov-race/lt-gov-robinson-announces-governor-bid/ |access-date=22 April 2023 |publisher=Fox 8 |date=22 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241112224742/https://myfox8.com/news/politics/nc-gov-race/lt-gov-robinson-announces-governor-bid/ |archive-date=November 12, 2024 |url-status=dead}}</ref> 

