[[Governor of Washington|Washington Governor]] [[Jay Inslee]] was re-elected to a third term in [[2020 Washington gubernatorial election|2020]] with 56.6% of the vote. Because [[Washington (state)|Washington]] does not have gubernatorial term limits in its [[Washington Constitution|constitution]], he was eligible to run for re-election for a fourth term, but he has decided not to seek re-election.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Furtado |first=David |date=2023-05-01 |title=Governor Inslee announces he will not seek re-election |url=https://keprtv.com/news/local/governor-inslee-announces-he-will-no-seek-re-election |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=KEPR |language=en}}</ref> [[Attorney General of Washington|State Attorney General]] [[Bob Ferguson (politician)|Bob Ferguson]] won the Democratic nomination.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-06-01 |title=What to know about state Sen. Mark Mullet as he joins race for WA governor |url=https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/politics/state-sen-mark-mullet-to-announce-bid-for-wa-governor/ |access-date=2023-07-15 |website=The Seattle Times |language=en-US|last=Withycombe |first=Claire}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-05-02 |title=WA Attorney General Bob Ferguson announces campaign for governor |url=https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/politics/wa-attorney-general-bob-ferguson-announces-campaign-for-governor/ |access-date=2023-07-15 |website=The Seattle Times |language=en-US|last1=Gutman |first1=David|last2=Brunner |first2=Jim}}</ref> In the Republican primary, former U.S. representative [[Dave Reichert]] won the nomination.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 7, 2023 |title=Dave Reichert wants to be state's 'servant' as governor |url=https://www.king5.com/article/news/politics/state-politics/dave-reichert-running-for-governor-ready-for-public-service/281-f71968eb-e89a-458f-b161-59aafe54538e |access-date=2023-07-18 |website=king5.com |language=en-US|last=Mikkelsen |first=Drew}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Sowersby |first=Shauna |date=November 11, 2022 |title=Controversial Richland school board member announces bid for Washington governor in 2024 |url=https://www.theolympian.com/news/local/article268638367.html |work=[[The Olympian]] |accessdate=May 3, 2024}}</ref>{{Election box begin no change|title=Blanket primary results<ref>{{cite web |title=Certification of Results |url=https://www.sos.wa.gov/sites/default/files/2024-08/Certification%20of%20Results%20-%202024%20Primary.pdf |website=Washington Secretary of State}}</ref>}}
