[[Governor of West Virginia|Governor]] [[Jim Justice]] was re-elected to a second term in [[2020 West Virginia gubernatorial election|2020]] with 63.5% of the vote. He was [[Term limits in the United States|term-limited]] by the [[West Virginia Constitution]] in 2024 and ineligible to seek re-election for a third consecutive term. Justice won the [[2024 United States Senate election in West Virginia]] and succeeded Joe Manchin.

[[West Virginia Attorney General|State Attorney General]] [[Patrick Morrisey]] won the Republican nomination, defeating former [[West Virginia House of Delegates|state Delegate]] [[Moore Capito]], businessman Chris Miller, and [[West Virginia Secretary of State|Secretary of State]] [[Mac Warner]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=McElhinny |first=Brad |date=2022-11-29 |title=Moore Capito, whose name likely rings a bell, says he's running for West Virginia governor |url=https://wvmetronews.com/2022/11/29/moore-capito-whose-name-likely-rings-a-bell-says-hes-running-for-west-virginia-governor/ |access-date=2023-07-18 |website=WV MetroNews |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="Miller">{{cite web |last1=Adams |first1=Steven |date=December 24, 2021 |title=Chris Miller, Son of Congresswoman Carol Miller, Announces 2024 Run for West Virginia Governor |url=https://www.theintelligencer.net/news/top-headlines/2021/12/chris-miller-son-of-congresswoman-carol-miller-announces-2024-run-for-west-virginia-governor/ |access-date=December 24, 2021 |website=[[The Intelligencer and Wheeling News Register|The Intelligencer. Wheeling-News Register]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2023-01-10 |title=W.Va. Secretary of State Mac Warner announces he will run for governor |url=https://wchstv.com/news/local/wva-secretary-of-state-mac-warner-announces-he-will-run-for-governor |access-date=2023-07-18 |website=WCHS |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |title=Patrick Morrisey wins Republican nomination for governor in West Virginia primary election |url=https://www.abc23.com/patrick-morrisey-wins-republican-nomination-for-governor-in-west-virginia-primary-election/ |website=ABC News |language=en|date=15 May 2024}}</ref>

[[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]] Mayor [[Stephen T. Williams|Steve Williams]] won the Democratic nomination unopposed.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Nolting |first=Mike |date=April 5, 2023 |title=Huntington mayor eyes run for governor as 'a climb worth taking' |work=[[West Virginia MetroNews]] |url=https://wvmetronews.com/2023/04/05/huntington-mayor-eyes-run-for-governor-as-a-climb-worth-taking/}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=September 4, 2023 |title=Steve Williams becomes 1st Democrat to enter West Virginia governor's race |work=[[Associated Press]] |url=https://apnews.com/article/steve-williams-west-virginia-governor-race-democrat-15e19c4376a400e67972ebed35bb4e8d |access-date=September 4, 2023}}</ref> 

Morrisey won the election in a [[landslide victory|landslide]] by over 30 points and managed to carry every single county.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://apnews.com/article/governor-west-virginia-patrick-morrisey-steve-williams-fe02206b30df78b1ffd83ddf39adf6a1 | title=Republican Morrisey wins West Virginia governor's race | website=[[Associated Press News]] | date=November 5, 2024 }}</ref>

